+### §6.3 Adaptive sizing and frozen RequiredSymbols(d)
+
+A timely REPLY_DIFF supplies uncensored start and now samples defined in §6.1. Each timely correlated REPLY_MATCH whose candidate proof verifies supplies one uncensored sizing observation with estimatedCurrentDifference=0 and estimatedRoundStartDifference=0. Include it in the same current-round and reusable round1 banks and the same resize as REPLY_DIFF samples, once per selected peer/slot; duplicates, late, invalid or stale replies add no sample. This prescribed zero is a sizing observation for MATCH, not proof that the raw admitted sets are equal. It requires no peeling, reconstruction, Ref add-back or retained cells. A fallback REPLY means either inbound decode did not succeed or a complete DIFF exceeded the message limit; apply the existing approximate estimator and growth rule to its cells. Every timely processed REPLY with cells records which residual cells are zero BEFORE peeling. Exclude index0 from the likelihood because p0=1; a zero symbol0 is used in the explicit zero-estimate branch below. For i>=1 use inclusionProbability=2/(i+2) and the model P(empty at i)=(1−inclusionProbability)^Delta. This is an independence approximation: schedule cells are correlated and mixed-sign cancellation is treated as negligible. Call the result the approximate maximum-likelihood estimate, not an exact MLE.
+
+Let L=max(number of distinct items decoded from this reply,abs(raw symbol0 count minus reference symbol0 count)). Maximize over integer Delta>=L:
+
+`emptyCellSum Delta*ln(1−inclusionProbability) + nonemptyCellSum ln(1−(1−inclusionProbability)^Delta)`.
+
+The stated objective is unimodal; search integer Delta in[L,2*M+P] with smaller-Delta tie breaking and stable log evaluation. If the maximizer would lie above the domain, record a censored result at L; never perform unbounded search. If all received nonzero-index cells are pre-peel empty and symbol0 residual is zero, estimatedDifference=0. If no received residual cell is empty before peeling, record a censored estimate with lowerSizingBound=max(L,InverseHalfCDF(m)), where m is the number of received cells and InverseHalfCDF(m) is the smallest nonnegative integer Delta with DifferenceCDF(Delta,m)<1/2. Apply this table-derived sizing floor rather than only the set-size/count difference. It is an empirical censoring floor, not authenticated set cardinality. For probe{0}, zero residual gives estimatedDifference=0; otherwise the censored floor is max(L,InverseHalfCDF(1)). The estimate is an approximation even on hostile input and never authenticates a set. Censored samples enter request selection at their lowerSizingBound; no floating-point estimates are rounded into different counts silently.
+
+InverseHalfCDF uses the frozen conservative step CDF and its specified extrapolation, not inverse linear median interpolation. Scan grid intervals for the first qualifying integer, since empirical rows need not be monotone across Delta; then use the monotone scaled4096 tail. The strict inequality excludes equality at1/2. Positive quantile lengths guarantee a finite inverse no greater than4096*m+1. A table-derived censor floor can exceed2*M+P on hostile input; record that censored floor without running an empty-domain MLE search or attributing a peer fault. Request lengths remain clipped to the existing cell cap. No new tuning constant or unbounded scan is added.
+
+For a fallback REPLY, compute two estimates. estimatedCurrentDifference uses the Ref captured at reply entry and sizes the next round. estimatedRoundStartDifference applies the same estimator after adding back the effect of items that entered Pending/Ref since round start, bounded by P, solely for estimation; it determines the next-height ratio. Neither estimate can mutate the peeler reference or produce extra body/evidence actions. Maintain a per-round list of additions to Ref still present at processing time, bounded by P. A/Pending transitions that leave membership unchanged are not recorded; removals drop the ID. Add back each listed item's encoding to the residual to undo its Ref subtraction. estimatedRoundStartDifference uses L=max(items decoded in the first attempt,absolute symbol0 count difference after add-back). If the list would exceed P, disable start estimation for the rest of that round and use estimatedCurrentDifference as its ratio sample instead; no penalty or abandonment. Charge the P-record list explicitly; no cross-round change log.
+
+The frozen table stores quantiles5%,10%,...,95% and100% of needed prefix length at each grid d. Let DifferenceCDF(d,n) be the conservative step CDF defined below. EstimatedDecodeProbability(n)=sampleMean DifferenceCDF(estimatedCurrentDifferenceAtSample,n). Candidate n values are the union of stored quantile lengths and S for current samples, each capped at maximumSymbolsPerReply: at most21*D values before deduplication. Minimize n/EstimatedDecodeProbability(n), ties to smaller n; for this cost comparison, positive n divided by zero is +infinity, so if every candidate has EstimatedDecodeProbability(n)=0 choose the smallest candidate and then apply the existing growth and cap rules. No usable samples with an existing prefix retain that prefix subject to the doubling floor below; without a prefix or usable round1 history, use the initial probe. A round with REPLY_MATCH or REPLY_DIFF samples sizes the next request from the combined samples using this normal estimator; n may shrink, including after an all-MATCH round. Only a round with no usable sizing samples retains the previous prefix n, such as an all-silent round. Recompute whenever usable samples exist; the result may happen to equal the prior value. The doubling triggers below are unchanged. Censored samples enter at their table-adjusted lowerSizingBound. Sort a censored sample above an uncensored sample of equal value when taking the upper median. Censoring triggers prefix growth, never a return to probe mode once a prefix exists.
+
+
+Censored/zero-decode escalation: remember the previous prefix request within the epoch for the conditional doubling floor; it is not an unconditional lower bound on later requests. Zero-decode doubling requires at least one fallback REPLY with cells, none of those replies succeeding on arrival/rescue, and no REPLY_MATCH or REPLY_DIFF success in that round. Both REPLY_MATCH and REPLY_DIFF count as completed sizing successes. Independently, a censored upper-median sizing sample triggers doubling. If either trigger holds and a prior prefix exists, choose nNext=min(cap,max(estimatorN,2*nPrevious)), with checked/saturating arithmetic; the estimator may choose more,never less. A round with no usable sizing samples keeps the previous prefix n; MATCH zero samples and DIFF samples use the same normal estimator and may shrink n when neither doubling trigger applies. No empty/no-cell round is called a zero-decode failure.
+
+Use the exponential probe only when this epoch has no prior prefix and no usable round1 history. For the first prefix after a probe: if its upper-median sample is censored or unusable, n=(largest probe index actually sent)+1, subject to the existing maximumSymbolsPerReply cap; otherwise use the estimator. This span is the prescribed transition operand, not authentication that all positions contain differences. Once the first prefix exists, apply the doubling rule from there and never return to probe mode within the epoch. This replaces the reported prefix/probe livelock without a new tuning constant.
+
+At a same-tip epoch rollover, clear current-round active sizing samples, prior-prefix and start-estimator additions; start with the ordinary initial probe, with no old-epoch sample reuse. Preserve the existing second bank containing this tip's epoch1-round1 observations for sizing epoch1-round1 after the next tip transition. Later epochs neither consult nor overwrite that bank; there is no third saved bank. First height probes. For new-height round1 apply the same empirical argmin to previous-height round1 samples individually scaled by |R|_now/|R|_then and rounded up. The scaled samples use the same upper-median censor ordering; they do not authorize returning to probe mode once a prefix exists. Previous |R|=0 or absent usable history permits a probe only when this epoch has no prior prefix. Record end-round1 |R| and r=median estimatedRoundStartDifference/|R| as a diagnostic; the sample-by-sample scaling, not a single median substitution, controls request sizing. Reorg/disconnect height transition uses available saved round1 information, otherwise probes.
